Apple today released HomeView Software 27.2, which is the software that runs on the upcoming HomeView device set to launch on November 13.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/homeview_home_screen_feature-1.jpg" alt="" width="2071" height="1165" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071442" /><br/>
The HomeView was announced earlier in October, but the early software release gives us a look at features like wallpapers and reveals a few tidbits we didn't previously know.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Wallpapers</h2><br/>
There are 20 default wallpapers to choose from on HomeView, with a range of colors. Users will also likely be able to set their own photo wallpaper. The HomeView uses faces, but the wallpapers may be shown on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/home-screen/">Home Screen</a>.<br/>
<br/>
