<br/>
<h2>Launcher</h2><br/>
Unlike iOS, HomeView doesn't use SpringBoard. It <a href="https://x.com/_inside/status/2116287497776832887">has a new launcher called BreadBoard</a>, and the process for its Control Center UI is called CupBoard.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>iOS 26</h2><br/>
There is a hidden HomeView Software 26 graphic in the update, which adds to evidence that Apple wanted to release the HomeView earlier but had to wait on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI. Apple also appears to have been testing the interface on a sixth-generation <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-mini/">iPad mini</a> before launch.<br/>
